  "body": "## Summary\n\nHosts arXiv:2605.06901, \"Reflections and New Directions for Human-Centered Large Language Models\" (Ziems, Zhao, Yang, et al., Stanford), as a literature-template example site. Built from the `self-evolving/literature-template` template using the **`paper-to-site`** skill.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `/` is the paper note and entry point — abstract, 8-chapter outline, source links.\n- Full text split into a section/subsection tree under `content/ziems2026reflections/` (eight chapters) with figures and the imported `bibliography.bib`.\n- LaTeX `sec:`/`subsec:`/`fig:` references rewritten into descriptive internal links.\n- `content/papers/` kept as the reference-note area; starter demo notes and sample papers removed.\n- **Root + section chrome:** relaxed `library-page`/`not-index` conditions (`quartz.ts`), dropped `folder.positions.right: []` so section indexes show the graph (`quartz.config.yaml`), and removed the `body[data-slug=\"index\"]` landing CSS (`custom.scss`) — so the root paper note and section indexes render like content pages (sidebar, header, graph, backlinks).\n\n## Validation\n\n- `npm run check` — tsc + prettier clean\n- `npm run build` — 34 pages, 99 files emitted\n\n## Deploy\n\nSet `SITE_URL` to the production domain. Vercel: framework **Other**, install `npm ci`, build `npm run build`, output `public`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
